msgid "SETTINGS_SAVE_BACKUPS_KEY"
msgstr "Keep save backups"

msgid "SETTINGS_SAVE_BACKUPS_HELP"
msgstr "Before a game's save (SRAM or EEPROM) is written back to its file, keep a copy of the old file in /NILESWAN/SAVES/<game>/, named after the date and time of the cartridge clock (or numbered if the clock is not set). This sets how many are kept per game; the oldest is deleted. Saves of the flash kind are not copied.\n\nStart > File > Restore save backup puts one back; the current save is copied first. Erase save data also keeps a copy, then asks whether to delete all the backups."

msgid "SETTINGS_SAVE_BACKUPS_OFF"
msgstr "Off"

msgid "SETTINGS_SAVE_BACKUPS_1"
msgstr "1"

msgid "SETTINGS_SAVE_BACKUPS_3"
msgstr "3"

msgid "SETTINGS_SAVE_BACKUPS_5"
msgstr "5"

msgid "SETTINGS_SAVE_MANAGE_KEY"
msgstr "Save data management"

msgid "SETTINGS_SAVE_MANAGE_HELP"
msgstr "Load a game's save data into the cartridge at launch and write it back to the storage card when the menu starts again. Turn it off when not running on the physical cartridge, where the save data comes back damaged: nothing is loaded and no save file is written."

msgid "SETTINGS_SAVE_ASK_BACKUP_KEY"
msgstr "Choose save at launch"

msgid "SETTINGS_SAVE_ASK_BACKUP_HELP"
msgstr "When a game with save backups is launched, ask which save to use: the current one (A on the first entry) or one of the backups. B goes back to the list."

msgid "SETTINGS_HIDE_NILESWAN_KEY"
msgstr "Hide NILESWAN folder"

msgid "SETTINGS_HIDE_NILESWAN_HELP"
msgstr "Leave the NILESWAN folder (menu files, settings, saves list, pictures...) out of the root folder's list (on by default). Turn this off to see it again."

msgid "SETTINGS_FAVORITES_KEY"
msgstr "Favorites & lists"

msgid "SETTINGS_FAVORITES_HELP"
msgstr "Where to show the Favorites, Recent and Most played lists.\n\n\"File list\": as folders at the top of the root folder.\n\"Start menu\": as entries of the Start menu.\n\"Off\": no lists, and launches are not recorded.\n\nY1 in the file list, or Start > File, adds or removes a favorite. Recent lists the last ROMs and patches launched; Most played the 20 launched most often. The status bar shows how many times a game was launched (and the date of the last launch, in Recent and Most played, if the cartridge clock is set). The statistics are kept in /NILESWAN/STATS.TXT."

msgid "SETTINGS_FAVORITES_FILE_LIST"
msgstr "File list"

msgid "SETTINGS_FAVORITES_START_MENU"
msgstr "Start menu"

msgid "SETTINGS_FAVORITES_OFF"
msgstr "Off"

msgid "SETTINGS_SCROLL_SPEED_KEY"
msgstr "Scroll speed"

msgid "SETTINGS_SCROLL_SPEED_HELP"
